<%- include('partials/header') %>

<div class="airbnb-layout" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1rem;">
  <div class="faq-section-header">
    <h1 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h1>
    <p class="faq-subtitle">
      Answers to common queries about Sparsh care pathways, payments, and patient security.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="faq-accordion">
    <details class="faq-item" open>
      <summary>
        <span>🔒 How is my anonymity protected?</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>
          When registering on Sparsh, patients can select the "Anonymous" registration checkbox. This hides your name and assigns a random placeholder identifier across all interfaces viewed by medical staff. Your email remains encrypted and is only used for system alerts.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>
        <span>⏰ What if I am past the 72-hour window for PEP?</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>
          If it has been more than 72 hours since potential exposure, PEP is generally not recommended as its effectiveness drops significantly. You should still book a general HIV counseling session immediately to outline testing timelines and discuss prevention options like PrEP.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>
        <span>🩺 Are the doctors on Sparsh licensed professionals?</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>
          Yes. All medical consultants and counselors on Sparsh undergo a verification process by our platform administrators. We verify qualifications, licensing registrations, and experience before activating their accounts on the dashboard.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>
        <span>💳 How does the billing and payment work?</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>
          Booking a consultation involves a nominal standard fee that goes directly to the counseling doctor. The booking system uses a simulated Razorpay and UPI checkout interface. You do not need real money to complete the simulation during this development stage.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details class="faq-item">
      <summary>
        <span>💊 How do I get my prescriptions?</span>
      </summary>
      <div class="faq-content">
        <p>
          Once a doctor completes your consultation, they will attach a digital prescription with detailed medication schedules directly to your appointment. You can view, download, or show it to your local pharmacy.
        </p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>
</div>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
